  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-13" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Organization, Business and Regulation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;WestGas InterState, Inc. (WGI) was incorporated in 1990 under the laws of Colorado. WGI is a small natural gas pipeline company engaged in transporting natural gas in interstate commerce under the authorization granted by and subject to the jurisdiction of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC) with respect to its gas operations, accounting policies and practices.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;WGI is a wholly owned subsidiary of Xcel Energy Inc. (Xcel Energy). Xcel Energy owns all the outstanding common stock of WGI. Xcel Energy Services Inc. (XES) is a service company for the Xcel Energy system and provides a variety of administrative, management, engineering, construction and corporate support services at cost, pursuant to a service agreement approved by the Securities and Exchange Commission under the Public Utility Holding Company Act. WGI has no employees and, accordingly, purchases operating and administrative services from XES and Public Service Company of Colorado (PSCo).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;WGI owns and operates an 11 mile interstate gas pipeline extending from the Chalk Bluffs Compressor Station located in Weld County, Colo., near the Colorado-Wyoming border to WGI&#8217;s Paraffin Meadows Meter Station located in Laramie County, Wyo., with a certificated service capacity of 13,674 Dekatherms (Dth) of natural gas per day. WGI operates the pipeline under the FERC&#8217;s optional certificate procedures. In general, the rates charged for service are based on the optimal designed use of the facilities with WGI assuming the economic risk associated with supply and demand.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The majority of the capacity of the pipeline has been contracted under firm contracts with one-year terms, which automatically renew on the anniversary date unless terminated by either party pursuant to the notification terms specified in the agreements. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Gas transportation revenues from customers were as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;padding-right:18pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:42.352%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.395%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:26.727%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.395%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:26.431%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#e0e0e0;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Black Hills Service Company, LLC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#e0e0e0;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#e0e0e0;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#e0e0e0;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;27,498&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#e0e0e0;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#e0e0e0;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#e0e0e0;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#e0e0e0;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;27,434&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#e0e0e0;border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#160;HollyFrontier Refining &amp;amp; Marketing LLC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;89,710&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;87,091&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#ffffff;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#e0e0e0;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Total&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#e0e0e0;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#e0e0e0;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#e0e0e0;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;117,208&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#e0e0e0;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#e0e0e0;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#e0e0e0;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#e0e0e0;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;114,525&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="background-color:#e0e0e0;border-bottom:3pt double #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Summary of Significant Accounting Policies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:115%"&gt;Cash Equivalents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;WGI considers investments in certain instruments, including all temporary cash investments, to be cash equivalents. These temporary cash investments are securities having original maturities of three months or less. The carrying amount of these investments approximates their fair value at Dec. 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:115%"&gt;Basis of Accounting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;The accompanying financial statements were prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC as set forth in the Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP). The following areas represent the significant differences between the Uniform System of Accounts and GAAP:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%;padding-left:15.13pt"&gt;Accumulated deferred income taxes are shown as long-term assets and liabilities at their gross amounts in the FERC presentation, in contrast to the GAAP presentation as net long-term assets and liabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%;padding-left:15.13pt"&gt;Various expenses such as donations, lobbying and other non-regulatory expenses are presented as other income and deductions for the FERC presentation and reported as operating expenses for the GAAP presentation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%;padding-left:15.13pt"&gt;Income tax expense is shown as a component of operating expense in the FERC presentation, in contrast to the GAAP presentation as a below-the-line deduction from operating income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;WGI revenues are generated from natural gas transportation services. Revenues for all services are based on the thermal quantity of gas delivered at a price specified in each individual contract. Firm transportation service has contracted reservation quantities that WGI recognizes as revenues over the contract life.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;For interruptible or firm quantity-based services, WGI records revenue when physical deliveries of natural gas are nominated to the agreed upon delivery point. WGI is subject to FERC regulations and, as a result, revenues collected may be subject to refund in a rate proceeding.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;Reserves are established for these potential refunds.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Property and Depreciation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Property is stated at original cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Provisions for depreciation of property, plant and equipment for financial accounting purposes are based on straight-line composite rates applied to the various classes of depreciable property. Depreciation rates include provisions for disposal and removal costs of property, plant and equipment. Depreciation and amortization expense, expressed as a percentage of average depreciable property, was approximately 0.81 and 0.33 percent for the years ended Dec. 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;For income tax purposes, WGI uses accelerated depreciation and other elections provided by tax laws. WGI has intangible property related to organizational costs of $150,476 for 2025 and 2024. The amortization period was 25 years. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:115%"&gt;Gas Imbalances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;WGI&#8217;s pipeline receives gas from PSCo and delivers gas to Black Hills Energy (BHE).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;The gas imbalances represent differences between actual deliveries between WGI and PSCo and/or WGI and BHE.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;Gas imbalances are recorded in Miscellaneous Current and Accrued Assets and Miscellaneous Current and Accrued Liabilities, as applicable, on the balance sheet and in Operation Expenses on the income statement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;WGI recorded an asset for the gas imbalance of $37,343 and $288,258 at Dec. 31, 2025 and 2024 respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;WGI operations are included in the consolidated federal and state income tax returns filed by Xcel Energy. The allocation of income tax consequences to WGI is calculated under a parent company policy which provides that benefits or liabilities created by WGI, computed on a separate return basis, will be allocated to (and paid to or by) WGI to the extent the benefits are usable or additional liabilities are incurred in Xcel Energy&#8217;s consolidated income tax returns.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;Deferred income taxes are provided for on temporary differences between the financial accounting and tax basis of assets and liabilities using tax rates that are scheduled to be in effect when the temporary differences are expected to reverse.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:115%"&gt;Comprehensive Income&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;For the years ended Dec. 31, 2025 and 2024, WGI had no other comprehensive income items; therefore, comprehensive income equals net income.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:115%"&gt;Subsequent Events &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%"&gt;Management has evaluated the impact of events occurring after Dec. 31, 2025 and has updated such evaluation for disclosure purposes through the date of this report. These statements contain all necessary adjustments and disclosures resulting from that evaluation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:115%"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Total income tax expense from operations differs from the amount computed by applying the statutory federal income tax rate to income before income tax expense. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Effective income tax reconciliation for years ended Dec. 31: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:69.435%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.395%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:13.036%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.395%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:13.039%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="display:none"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#e0e0e0;pad